    "U+200D (ZWJ) and U+FE0F (VS16) are not covered by the core Unicode 15 width table, so the recovery parser replaces each with U+FFFD; the record-only ZWJ/keycap sample is parsed as U+1F469 U+FFFD U+1F4BB '1' U+FFFD U+20E3. Recorded only; no clustering or width policy is approved.",
    "Segoe UI Emoji advances 21 px in an 18 px (two-cell) span; the unclipped reference ink is 3..17 px and the painted ink is also 3..17 px, so these two scalars are not visibly clipped. This is not generalised to other emoji.",
    "The offscreen platform only loads the host font faces after QT_QPA_FONTDIR points at %WINDIR%/Fonts; without them the test records host_fallback_rendered=false instead of passing a glyph check."
